---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
---
<Layout title="About" description="BhaktiMedia — why we exist, what we believe, and the promise we make to every temple and creator we work with.">

<!-- ═══ HERO ══ -->
<section class="relative overflow-hidden pb-16 pt-32 text-center">
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-24 left-1/2 h-96 w-[160%] -translate-x-1/2 bg-gradient-to-b from-saffron/10 to-transparent blur-2xl"></div>
  <span class="pointer-events-none absolute right-8 top-24 select-none font-dev text-[140px] text-saffron/5">ॐ</span>
  <div class="container-x relative px-4 sm:px-6">
    <span class="chip bg-saffron/10 text-saffron">🪔 About BhaktiMedia</span>
    <h1 class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-5xl xl:text-6xl">
      We Believe Devotion Deserves <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-saffron to-golden bg-clip-text text-transparent">Great Design</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 font-dev text-sm text-goldsoft">॥ श्रद्धावान् लभते ज्ञानम् ॥</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ STORY ═══ -->
<section class="section !pt-4">
  <div class="container-x grid gap-10 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_360px]">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Our Story</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">How BhaktiMedia Started</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/80 dark:text-cream/70">
        BhaktiMedia began with a simple observation: temples, trusts, and devotional creators across India were producing some of the most meaningful content on the internet — and almost none of it looked, sounded, or performed the way it deserved to.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/80 dark:text-cream/70">
        Aarti livestreams recorded on shaky phones. Festival posters designed in ten minutes the night before Ganesh Chaturthi. YouTube channels with powerful content buried under thumbnails no one clicked on. <b class="text-ink dark:text-cream">The devotion was never the problem. The craft around it was missing.</b>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/80 dark:text-cream/70">
        So we built a team that sits exactly at that intersection — people who understand both design and devotion, both algorithms and aartis. Not an agency that occasionally takes on a "temple project," but one whose entire practice is built around this one world.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="grid content-start gap-4">
      <div class="card p-5 shadow-soft">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we saw</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2.5 text-sm text-sandal-deep/70 dark:text-cream/60">
          <li>📱 Aarti livestreams on shaky phones</li>
          <li>🌙 Posters made at 10 PM the night before</li>
          <li>📉 Great content, unclicked thumbnails</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card border-2 border-saffron/40 p-5 shadow-gold">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we built</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/70 dark:text-cream/60">
          A team at the intersection of <b>design & devotion</b>, <b>algorithms & aartis</b> — whose entire practice is built around this one world.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ BELIEFS ═══ -->
<section class="section !pt-0">
  <div class="container-x px-4 sm:px-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our Philosophy</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What We Believe</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card relative overflow-hidden p-6 shadow-soft">
        <span class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-4 -top-4 text-[90px] opacity-[0.07]">🪔</span>
        <span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-saffron to-golden text-2xl text-white shadow-gold">🪔</span>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-lg font-bold">Tradition × Technology</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/70 dark:text-cream/60">
          Tradition and technology aren't in tension. A festival poster generated with AI can be just as respectful, accurate, and moving as one hand-painted — if the people building it understand what they're depicting and why it matters.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card relative overflow-hidden p-6 shadow-soft">
        <span class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-4 -top-4 text-[90px] opacity-[0.07]">🔍</span>
        <span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-saffron to-golden text-2xl text-white shadow-gold">🔍</span>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-lg font-bold">Detail is a Form of Respect</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/70 dark:text-cream/60">
          The mudra of a hand, the placement of a tilak, the correct associated colors for a devta, the right time-of-day glow for an aarti scene — we treat these as non-negotiable, not decorative.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card relative overflow-hidden p-6 shadow-soft">
        <span class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-4 -top-4 text-[90px] opacity-[0.07]">🌐</span>
        <span class="grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-saffron to-golden text-2xl text-white shadow-gold">🌐</span>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-lg font-bold">Reach is a Form of Seva</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/70 dark:text-cream/60">
          A temple's digital presence isn't vanity metrics. It's the difference between a devotee who moved abroad still being able to join the Tuesday aarti, or a homebound elder still hearing their favorite bhajan live.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ WHAT WE DO ═══ -->
<section class="section !pt-0">
  <div class="container-x px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="card p-7 shadow-soft sm:p-9">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our Craft</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What We Do</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/80 dark:text-cream/70">
        From devotional poster design and AI-generated deity art, to full temple branding, YouTube channel management, cinematic aarti films, Bhakti reels, voiceovers in Marathi, Hindi, Sanskrit and English, and complete digital identity systems — we cover the full range of what a temple or devotional creator needs to show up beautifully online.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {["Devotional Posters", "Temple Branding", "YouTube Management", "AI Image Generation", "Video Editing", "Bhakti Reels", "Voiceovers", "Thumbnail Design", "Social Media", "Website Design"].map((s) => (
          <span class="chip bg-sandal/10 text-sandal-deep dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-cream/60">{s}</span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 border-l-4 border-saffron pl-4 text-sm font-semibold text-sandal-deep/80 dark:text-cream/70">
        Every project starts the same way: understanding the tradition first, the platform second.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ WHO WE WORK WITH ═══ -->
<section class="section !pt-0">
  <div class="container-x px-4 sm:px-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our Family</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Who We Work With</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-sandal-deep/80 dark:text-cream/70">
      We work with temple trusts, utsav committees, devotional YouTubers, and independent spiritual creators across India — from long-established mandirs with decades of history to newer creators building a following one reel at a time. What they share is a desire to represent their devotion with the same care they'd bring to the sanctum itself.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {[
        { icon: "🛕", t: "Temple Trusts", d: "Decades-old mandirs going digital" },
        { icon: "🎪", t: "Utsav Committees", d: "Festival campaigns that reach thousands" },
        { icon: "📺", t: "Devotional YouTubers", d: "Channels built on bhakti content" },
        { icon: "✨", t: "Spiritual Creators", d: "One reel at a time, with intention" },
      ].map((w) => (
        <div class="card p-5 text-center shadow-soft transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift">
          <span class="text-3xl">{w.icon}</span>
          <p class="mt-2 font-display text-sm font-bold">{w.t}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-sandal-deep/60 dark:text-cream/50">{w.d}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══ OUR PROMISE ═══ -->
<section class="section !pt-0">
  <div class="container-x px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-ink to-[#3a2410] p-8 text-cream shadow-lift dark:from-night-soft dark:to-black sm:p-12">
      <span class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-8 -top-8 select-none font-dev text-[160px] text-golden/5">॥</span>
      <p class="eyebrow !text-goldsoft">Our Promise</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What We Will Never Do</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cream/80 sm:text-base">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-golden">🪔</span> We won't rush a deity's likeness to hit a deadline.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-golden">🪔</span> We won't reuse a design across traditions that don't share it.</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-golden">🪔</span> We'll always tell you honestly if something isn't ready to publish.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl border-l-4 border-golden pl-4 text-sm italic text-cream/70">
        ...because what we make carries someone's faith, and that isn't something we take lightly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<CTA />
</Layout>